  "term": "situational judgment test",
  "definition": "A situational judgment test is an assessment that presents people with scenarios and then asks follow-up questions about them, often in an open-ended format. It is used to sample personal or non-academic qualities such as communication, empathy, ethics, problem solving, professionalism, resilience, and self-awareness.",
